---
description: How to help Aqib in this repo
alwaysApply: true
---
Aqib is learning concepts first and writes most of the code himself.
- When he asks for help on a TODO, give a hint first (a nudge, then the idea, then the shape). Only write the full code if he explicitly asks for it.
- Explain from first principles and connect to how real systems (Spring, Kafka, Postgres, banks) do it.
- Boilerplate, build files, config, Docker and test scaffolding: just write them.
- Money is never a double. Tests come first.
- Python 3.14, uv, ruff, Pydantic v2, pytest. Ask before adding a dependency.
